{"full":"hf:EmilyWitko/May2024_HugginessSurveyResults","spaceId":"EmilyWitko/May2024_HugginessSurveyResults","name":"May 2024 Hugginess Survey Results","source":"huggingface","description":"An interactive AI application on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"HTML","topics":["static","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":6,"created":"2024-06-18T03:26:17.000Z","updated":"2024-06-18T22:06:50.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://emilywitko-may2024-hugginesssurveyresults.static.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/EmilyWitko/May2024_HugginessSurveyResults","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:10.191Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:10.191Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:10.191Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🤗","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I want to extend my gratitude to everyone who participated in this survey – your feedback is invaluable. 64% of you sent us your thoughts (58% is our average response rate). As always, if your perspective differs from the majority, please know that we value your viewpoint and are excited to make Hugging Face an even better place to work. Meg said it best when she said, “We disagree, but still respect one another and work towards a shared alignment on priorities.” Your voice matters to me and to Hugging Face.","As we’ve seen in previous surveys, we greatly value the autonomy and freedom we experience at Hugging Face, along with the supportiveness and empathy within our teams. Additionally, work-life balance, the competence of our colleagues, and the opportunity to work on impactful projects are major positives. Since our last Hugginess Survey (October 2023), we’re excited to share that there are fewer concerns about the vision and direction of Hugging Face, and folks are feeling more clarity about their projects. Conversely, concerns about compensation, professional development, and belonging exist.…","A note on underrepresentation in tech: I also want to offer a special additional thank you for answering the question regarding underrepresentation in tech. We’ll use your self-identification to break down the survey answers a bit further. Watch out for the numbers in blue to see how our underrepresented voices responded to each question."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/EmilyWitko/May2024_HugginessSurveyResults/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"affbdce0fdf5ed58de4a0cdb0ab4fdbc6c29f6602a569700dd7c7939896dbe33","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:10.275Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:10.275Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"I want to extend my gratitude to everyone who participated in this survey – your feedback is invaluable. 64% of you sent us your thoughts (58% is our average response rate). As always, if your perspective differs from the majority, please know that we value your viewpoint and are excited to make Hugging Face an even better place to work. Meg said it best when she said, “We disagree, but still respect one another and work towards a shared alignment on priorities.” Your voice matters to me and to Hugging Face.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/EmilyWitko/May2024_HugginessSurveyResults/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"affbdce0fdf5ed58de4a0cdb0ab4fdbc6c29f6602a569700dd7c7939896dbe33","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/EmilyWitko/May2024_HugginessSurveyResults/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:10.275Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-06-18T22:06:50.000Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/EmilyWitko/May2024_HugginessSurveyResults/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T11:06:10.275Z","hash":"affbdce0fdf5ed58de4a0cdb0ab4fdbc6c29f6602a569700dd7c7939896dbe33","originalBytes":10743,"storedBytes":10743,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["team","work","hugging","nps","face","